Top-level identifiers in the peacemakers scene are renamed with unique prefixes, and the far-layer blur calculation is capped at 0.9 px.

Every scene script runs in the shared global lexical scope without module isolation. Renaming `LAYERS` and generic hook functions prevents cross-script SyntaxError collisions on merge, while the blur cap preserves text readability during actor entrance scaling.

### Changes made
1. In [`peacemakers.js`](file://$HOME/.claude/worktrees/mothers-love-tv-peacemakers/public/color-polish/scenes/peacemakers.js):
   - Renamed `LAYERS` to `PEACEMAKERS_LAYERS` across definitions and hook references.
   - Renamed helper functions `place`, `mount`, and `integrate` to `placePEACEMAKERS`, `mountPEACEMAKERS`, and `integratePEACEMAKERS` (with `peacemakersPlace`, `peacemakersMount`, and `peacemakersIntegrate` aliases).
   - Updated the scene registration descriptor to reference the prefixed hook functions.
   - Capped the blur calculation in `placePEACEMAKERS` to `Math.min(.9, Math.max(baseBlur, L.blur))`.
2. In [`peacemakers.md`](file://$HOME/.claude/worktrees/mothers-love-tv-peacemakers/docs/runs/2026-09-11-tv-scenes/lanes/peacemakers.md):
   - Appended the round r2 completion record line to `## Result`.

